specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:165:Requests conversation summaries for the user authenticated when this socket was upgraded. The server MUST take the user id from the connection and MUST ignore any `userId` supplied in the frame. The request is answered independently of a streaming turn; it does not enter the per-session message queue. ([validated by: asks the session store for the authenticated session user when listing sessions](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L91))
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:182:When present, `before` MUST contain both fields. Invalid pagination is answered with `INVALID_MESSAGE`; fields outside this wire shape are ignored. ([validated by: validates list_sessions pagination and strips fields outside its wire shape](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L24))
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:361:Answers `list_sessions` with metadata for the socket's authenticated user's conversations. It contains no conversation entries or other conversation content. Dates are ISO-8601 strings on the wire. A store without `listFor` answers an empty list; a store failure answers `SERVER_ERROR` and does not close the socket. ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L134))
